1 FAMS @F71@
1 NOTE Professor of Hebrew language and Hebrew literature. Israel Prize for linquistics and Hebrew language 1985
2 CONT
2 CONT Yehoshua Blau (Hebrew: יהושע בלאו , September 22, 1919 – October 20, 2020) was an Israeli scholar of Arabic language and literature, previously Professor Emeritus at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem
2 CONT
2 CONT Blau was born in Cluj, Romania in September 1919. He moved to Mandatory Palestine with his family in 1938. He earned a master's degree in Hebrew, Arabic, and Biblical studies in 1942. He married Shulamit in 1945, and they had a son and daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yehoshua_Blau
2 CONT
2 CONT Honorary Member - Royal Asiatic Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Association of Jewish Libraries RAS Division Reference Award 2007.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.timesofisrael.com/prof-yehoshua-blau-giant-of-semitic-l...
2 CONT
2 CONT Jehosua Blau
2 CONT
2 CONT Mandatory Palestine Naturalization Applications, 1937-1947
2 CONT Hebrew name:יהושע בלאו
2 CONT Birth:Sep 22 1919 - Cluj, Romania
2 CONT Naturalization:May 15 1941
